# Build context for sim/Dockerfile and detect/Dockerfile (also the CDK DockerImageAsset fingerprints).
# Allowlist: the images need only the lock files, facility/, sim/ and detect/. Each CDK image asset
# also excludes the other image's code, so a change to one never rebuilds the other.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!facility
!sim
!detect

# Never in the context, even if the allowlist grows.
.venv
.git
cdk.out
_bmad*
.work
tests
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
